  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the **MPStorage thread** to stay out of my MP list and out of my unread count: subject `a2bcc09b796b8c6fab77058ff8446c34`, recipient « MultiMP ». It is the technical store the HFR+ clients use for flags, bookmarks and the synced blacklist, not a conversation. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17: it shows in Messages, marked « non lu ».)\n\n### Today\n\n- dev-swift shows it as a normal row in Messages › « MP » (screenshot 2026-11-17), often as **non lu**: every write by any client (iOS, DTCloud, userscripts) bumps it.\n- Legacy @ 87fe0d1c shows it too: `MPListView.swift` has no filter, and `MP_NAME` is only used by `Classes/MPStorage.m:23, 713, 820` to find or create it. Hiding it is therefore a **deliberate gap** (operator).\n- The match already exists: `MPStoragePageParser.isStorageSubject` (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRParsing/MPStorage/MPStoragePageParser.swift:86-88`), the whole title with or without `[non lu] `, as legacy `:713`.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Hide the storage thread from the MP list (« MP » and « MP multiples »), using `isStorageSubject` rather than a second matcher.\n2. It does not count in the unread MP figures:\n   - the Messages tab badge;\n   - the app icon badge (LOT-140);\n   - the background check's notification;\n   - the « MP multiples » counts.\n   If HFR's own unread count (the header) includes it, decide from a capture or from the legacy code; do not guess. If the HFR count cannot be corrected safely, say so on this issue.\n3. MPStorage reads and writes are unchanged: they find the thread by scanning the list pages themselves (LOT-038/052).\n4. Whether a switch shows it again: none unless the operator asks.\n5. Add a ledger `gap-new` row.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- List tests on a fixture with the storage row, unread and read: it is not in the displayed list, and the unread count leaves it out.\n- An MPStorage transport test still finds the thread.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nMessages: no « a2bcc09b… » row, and the badge leaves it out.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
